feat(roadmap): schema expansion for Jira-forward + team-ready coordination (ADR-0036)

Extend roadmap_items with the structural surface area markdown carried but the
tuple-projected table couldn't: split-content (title/why/next-cut/description),
hierarchy (parent_id/ordering), 4-valued visibility, four timeline fields, and
nullable team_id/workspace_id/workflow_id for the eventual multi-tenant story.

Status becomes an open string so team-defined workflows ("blocked", "in-review")
round-trip; the six built-in values still sort first via a known-rank table.
Adds `quarantined` as a sixth canonical status for un-spider findings.

New relational tables (projections + relations, tuples remain the write log):

  - roadmap_item_edges     : blocks/depends-on/parent-of/relates-to/duplicates
  - roadmap_item_owners    : principal_type × principal_id × role
  - roadmap_item_artifacts : PRs, ADRs, screenshots, operator-quotes
  - roadmap_item_tags      : free-form labels
  - roadmap_item_events    : append-only audit timeline (auto-minted on writes)

Fourteen new factory APIs (addEdge/removeEdge/listEdges, addOwner/…,
addArtifact/…, addTag/…, addEvent/events) all guard `relationalOrThrow()` so
callers without a SQLite handle get a clear error instead of a silent no-op.
Relational writes auto-mint events; events are the cheap way to ask "what
happened to this item" without replaying the global tuple log.

Cartographer remains the sole authoritative writer of status (via tuples);
nothing in this PR changes that contract.

PR-β (next) carries the markdown→DB migration, read-path rewires (cartographer
prompt, getRoadmapProgress, `pd roadmap` CLI, website docs surface), and the
file deletions. ADR-0036 documents the split.

Tests: 14 new in roadmap-items.test.js covering content split, legacy
summaryMd fallback, hierarchy, team-forward fields, timeline fields, arbitrary
status strings, and all 14 relational APIs (incl. no-db throw guards).
All 82 unit tests across roadmap-items/promote/pop/cartographer-routes pass.
`tsc --noEmit` clean.


